IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc-interpretation`

-- ccc-interpretation-tests.l4 -- tests for ccc-interpretation.l4 (sections 1, 2.2, 2.3, 3, 3.01).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the provision (quoted in ccc-interpretation.l4), before the run,
-- never copied from the encoding's output. JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered.

§ `Tests for section 1`

#ASSERT `s 1 the short title` EQUALS "Criminal Code"

§ `Tests for section 2.2`

-- 2.2(1): each of the five relations, for a listed purpose, when the victim is dead (and, separately, when the victim is incapable).
--   columns of the call: the relation | the purpose (a section) | the victim is dead | the victim is incapable of acting
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `the victim’s spouse, or if the victim is dead, their spouse at the time of death` (`Provision of the Code` OF 606, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `the victim’s common-law partner, or if the victim is dead, their common-law partner at the time of death` (`Provision of the Code` OF 606, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of a dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each of the six sections it is for the purposes of, and the sections on either side of two of them.
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 672.5, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.37, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 737.1, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 745.63, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 605, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 721, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 745.6, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "If the victim is dead or incapable of acting": neither, and the answer is no (a failed "if": a marginal reading).
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `an individual with none of those relations to the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An individual with none of the five relations: the list is not closed, so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `an individual with none of those relations to the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 2.2(2): barred if an accused, found guilty, or found not criminally responsible or unfit; otherwise the text's "if" is not met.
--   columns: an accused in relation to the offence | found guilty of it | found not criminally responsible or unfit in respect of it
#ASSERT `s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 2.2(1) and (2) together.
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The two real functions composed: a relative of a dead victim, for s 722, who is the accused in the offence: barred; who is not: may act.
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` (`s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") TRUE FALSE) (`s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` (`s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` `a relative or dependant of the victim` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") TRUE FALSE) (`s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests for section 2.3`

-- Helpers for the cases below (test-local names): a charge under a section and subsection with every other fact false, and a case under a section for the UN personnel limb.
--   columns of the facts: the offence charged | terrorism offence (s 2) | against UN or associated personnel | 7(3.71) | (c) outside Canada, deemed in Canada | (d) terrorist activity (b), deemed by 7(3.74) or (3.75) | (e) s 811 with consent | the section the proceedings are under
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings`
`test case: charged under` MEANS `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")

GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      un IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings`
`test case: against UN personnel` MEANS `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF sec, ""), (JUST FALSE), un, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")

GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings`
`test case: proceedings under` MEANS `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF sec, "")

-- 2.3(1)(a): the sections, each; the s 7 subsections, each; and the sections next to them.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 57 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 58 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 83.12 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 103 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 104 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 121.1 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 380 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 382 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 382.1 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 391 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 400 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 424.1 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 431.1 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 467.11 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 467.111 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.01)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.3)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.31)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.35)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.36)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "(2.4)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 7 "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 56 "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 381 "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 467.12 "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2.3(1)(a), "or in relation to any terrorism offence": the answer of s 2 "terrorism offence" decides.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 380.5, ""), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 380.5, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 380.5, ""), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2.3(1)(b): an offence against UN or associated personnel under 235, 236, 266 to 269, 269.1, 271 to 273, 279, 279.1 (the sections inside and just outside each range).
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 235 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 236 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 265 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 266 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 267 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
