#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 269 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 269.01 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 269.1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 270 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 271 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 272 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 273 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 273.1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 279 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 279.1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: against UN personnel` 266 FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2.3(1)(c), (d), (e): the flags.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 1, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 1, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 1, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 811, ""), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (`Provision of the Code` OF 0, "")) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2.3(1)(f): proceedings under section 83.13, 83.14, 83.222, 83.223 or 83.3.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.13) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.222) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.223) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: proceedings under` 83.2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Section 2 "Attorney General" (a): proceedings referred to in 2.3(1) have the Attorney General of Canada as well as the province's.
`a fraud prosecution (s 380) under the Code in a province` MEANS `s 2 Attorney General: facts of the proceedings` OF TRUE, (`s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 380 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a theft prosecution (s 334) under the Code in a province` MEANS `s 2 Attorney General: facts of the proceedings` OF TRUE, (`s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` (`test case: charged under` 334 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 Attorney General` `a fraud prosecution (s 380) under the Code in a province` EQUALS JUST (LIST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`, `the Attorney General of Canada`)
#ASSERT `s 2 Attorney General` `a theft prosecution (s 334) under the Code in a province` EQUALS JUST (LIST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`)

-- 2.3(2): the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the Attorney General's powers in respect of an offence in (1) or under another Act of Parliament.
--   columns: the answer of s 2.3(1) | the offence is under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act, or a regulation under one
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2.3(2)(a) to (f): the proceedings those powers include; any other kind is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding for conspiring or attempting to commit such an offence or for being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding in relation to a criminal organization offence that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding in relation to an offence referred to in section 354, 355.2, 355.4 or 462.31 that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding or out of any act or omission that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding for the breach of any court order made in the course of a proceeding commenced or conducted by the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding for the failure to comply with any condition associated with the release of a person by a peace officer or other competent authority, including a condition to appear at a specified time and place, in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `any ancillary proceedings in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` `a proceeding of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 2.3(3): the Director of Public Prosecutions, for an offence under the Canada Elections Act.
#ASSERT `s 2.3(3) the Director of Public Prosecutions exercises the powers and performs the duties and functions of the Attorney General of Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2.3(3) the Director of Public Prosecutions exercises the powers and performs the duties and functions of the Attorney General of Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 3`

-- 3: all four limbs, and each limb failing in turn.
--   columns: in a provision of this Act | a reference to another provision or another Act | followed by words in parenthesis | descriptive or purporting to be
#ASSERT `s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` (`s 3 reference` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` (`s 3 reference` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` (`s 3 reference` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` (`s 3 reference` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` (`s 3 reference` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for section 3.01`

-- 3.01(2): each provision on the list, and the neighbours that are not on it. Section 726.21 is listed as a whole section.
#ASSERT `s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 109, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 109, "(2)") EQUALS NOTHING
